The sky appears blue because of a phenomenon called Ray optics, where sunlight interacts with the Earth's atmosphere. When sunlight enters the atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules and small particles, causing some of the light to scatter in all directions. This scattered light reaches our eyes, making the sky appear blue. [end of text]


